The first matrix (let's call it M) is:

\[
M = \begin{pmatrix}
0 & c & -b \\
-c & 0 & a \\
b & -a & 0
\end{pmatrix}
\]

The second matrix (let's call it N) is:

\[
N = \begin{pmatrix}
a^2 & ab & ac \\
ab & b^2 & bc \\
ac & bc & c^2
\end{pmatrix}
\]

The task is to compute M × N and check if it's the zero matrix. Let me recall that matrix multiplication involves taking the dot product of rows from the first matrix with columns from the second matrix. Each element (i,j) of the resulting matrix is the sum of M[i,k] * N[k,j] for k from 1 to 3.

