To determine the number of elements in the set \( A = \{x \in S \mid x \text{ is a solution to } x^2 = 2\} \), we start by analyzing the equation \( x^2 = 2 \). Here, \( x \) is a vector in \( \mathbb{R}^n \), so the equation must hold component-wise. 

For each coordinate \( x_i \) of the vector \( x \), the equation \( (x_i)^2 = 1 \) must be satisfied. This implies that each coordinate \( x_i \) must be either \( 1 \) or \( -1 \). Therefore, the set \( A \) consists of all vectors in \( \mathbb{R}^n \) where each coordinate is either \( 1 \) or \( -1 \).

Since there are \( n \) coordinates in the vector and each coordinate has 2 possible values (\( 1 \) or \( -1 \)), the total number of elements in \( A \) is \( 2^n \).

Thus, the number of elements in the set \( A \) is \(\boxed{2^n}\).
