**Teaching the Core Concept:**  
The binomial coefficient \( \dbinom{14}{11} \) is calculated as follows:  
\[
\dbinom{14}{11} = \frac{14!}{11! \cdot (14-11)!} = \frac{14 \times 13 \times 12}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 364
\]  
Ensure the student understands combinatorial calculations and practice with similar problems to build confidence in numerical computations.
