Q: META-MATH: Find the $2 \times 2$ matrix $\mathbf{M}$ such that $\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ 21 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} X \\ -17 \end{pmatrix}.$
If we know the answer to the above question is \begin{pmatrix}2&1\7&-2\end{pmatrix}, what is the value of unknown variable X?
