**Explanation:**  
The problem requires finding the value of \( X \) in the second condition of the matrix equation. Given the correct matrix \( \mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 1 \\ 7 & -2 \end{pmatrix} \), compute \( \mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix} \):  
\[
\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 1 \\ 7 & -2 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} (2)(-1) + (1)(5) \\ (7)(-1) + (-2)(5) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -17 \end{pmatrix}.
