### **Explanation of Correct Answer**  
The matrix transformation’s area scaling factor is determined by the **determinant** of the matrix:  
\[
\text{det}\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\ 7 & -3\end{bmatrix} = (2)(-3) - (1)(7) = -6 - 7 = -13.
\]  
The absolute value of the determinant is \( |{-13}| = 13 \). The transformed area is:  
\[
\text{Original Area} \times \text{Determinant} = 10 \times 13 = 130.
\]  

