Each term is log2((n+1)/n) where n starts at 1 and goes up to 2009. So the product inside the log would be (2/1) * (3/2) * (4/3) * ... * (2010/2009). 

Notice that in this product, each numerator cancels with the denominator of the next term. For example, the 2 in the numerator of the first term cancels with the 2 in the denominator of the second term. Similarly, the 3 in the numerator of the second term cancels with the 3 in the denominator of the third term, and so on. This telescoping product means that almost all terms cancel out except the first denominator and the last numerator. 

